s for the book  and then I choose 20 from from that and  I was so pleasantly surprised because my  email box was literally jammed with  email messages for more than 200 women  who wanted to tell me about their  internet business and it was just so  neat to see that there was that level of  entrepreneurial activity happening out  there by women and since then I've and  looking at numbers and statistics a  little bit more there is a statistic  that shows that women are starting  businesses at a rate twice that of the  national average so a lot of  entrepreneurial activity by women  happening these days and let's see here  with with the book how he ended up  structuring it is that each chapter  focuses on a different entrepreneur and  her business and I picked the  entrepreneurs with an eye to variety i  was looking for entrepreneurs with very  different backgrounds so some of these  women come from working-class family  some come from wealthy families some  have mba summer technologists a lot of  different types of backgrounds two of  the companies are located outside of the  united states ones in sao paulo and ones  in tokyo and i also picked businesses  that are in very different market  segments so just a lot of variety and  the types of businesses and i want to  tell you a little bit about a couple of  the entrepreneurs in the book and  Eugenie de serio is one of them and  she's the founder of a company called  astronaut and at the time that she got  her business idea she was she was kind  of down on her luck she had been through  a bad breakup she was a single mom she  was unemployed she lost her job and she  kind of been forced because of financial  reasons to move back in with her mom and  dad so she was living at home and trying  to figure out what she would do next and  she had a long-standing passion which  was astrology and so she started writing  horoscopes and she decided that she  start publishing these things online and  at that time it was back in 1994