about writing a book that i've  discovered is that a couple of weeks  after the books been out and people have  seen it and started to read it is you  start to get these kind of random emails  from people who want to ask you a  question or say something to you and I  got one about three weeks ago that  really made my day and I wanted to read  it to you see if I can find it here I  know it's here and my stack of papers  here it is it says hi my name is Ashley  and I'm thinking of starting an Internet  company either a web design company or a  company that sells clipart on CD ROMs  what should I consider in making the  decision I'm excellent with websites  HTML and animated banner design now  here's the punch line she goes on to say  I'm 12 will this be a problem i've heard  there are some 13 and over laws thanks  Ashley well I got this email and I  thought that was so cool i thought you  know any girl like Ashley she's going to  go really far in life and it really made  me think that you know the more that we  can do to encourage girls to feel at  home in the technology arena the more  that we can encourage girls to feel at  home in the business world the better  off we're all going to be in the  handouts you have toward the back it's I  think it's the third to last page there  are a list of resources there for  entrepreneurs and I picked out a few of  the resources from dot com divas in the  book there is a resource appendix that  lists a lot of different types of  resources funding sources for  entrepreneurs especially for women  entrepreneurs organizations that help  women entrepreneurs websites etc there's  a lot of good stuff in there but for  those of you who don't buy the book you  at least get the cliff note version  there in the handout and one of these  sources that I just want to mention  because it is a very useful one is  venturewire and at venturewire you can  subscribe to an email list it's free and  it gives a daily email message that  summarizes what